      "SUBCLINICAL INFECTION RUINS EXPERIMENTAL DATA even when it kills nothing, by altering immune responses, growth, enzyme levels and organ weights — this is why health monitoring exists.",
      "TYZZER'S DISEASE = CLOSTRIDIUM PILIFORME (formerly Bacillus piliformis) — a Gram-negative to Gram-variable, SPORE-FORMING, OBLIGATE INTRACELLULAR, long FILAMENTOUS rod.",
      "IT CANNOT BE GROWN ON ORDINARY MEDIA — routine culture is ALWAYS NEGATIVE. Diagnosis rests entirely on HISTOPATHOLOGY.",
